## 1. inputs and result

the precise inputs are:

- **i-pc:** [pc1-pc5 and pc11](../[research revision]-continuation/physical-covariance.md), including the actual normalized gauss kernels, primitive relative character, natural zero extensions, mixed embedding map, and absolute complete-zero estimate.
- **i-fr:** [fr3-fr19](../[research revision]/physical-forced-rows.md), especially the weighted fixed-radical mass for every fixed divisor exponent strictly greater than \(1/6\). the particular mass statement used is restated in (ph8); it is an accepted input, not silently strengthened.
- **i-hc:** [hc7-hc18](../[research revision]/physical-radical-mass.md), used to prove the restricted exponent-zero mass in section 4.
- **i-sextic:** the actual fields, original marks, original profiles and polynomial scale ranges in [t06-t07](../[research revision]/[restricted mathematical source]#t06-the-complete-same-core-sextic-square-function).
- for the separate active-conductor comparison only, the exact single-source reduction and coefficient count in [xm13-xm30](../[research revision]/mixed-linear-transfer.md#4-exact-reduction-of-every-source-power).

ordinary smooth character poisson is sufficient. no new i-hecke, i-zeta, dedekind nonvanishing, or higher moment estimate is assumed. the stronger inherited i-hecke input is still needed if one separately invokes t07's strongest large-true-gcd tail.

keep the exact parameters
